quiz 3 | "It was a bright cold day in April, and the clocks were striking thirteen." Which novel?
* Nineteen Eighty-Four
o Brave New World
o Fahrenheit 451
o The Handmaid's Tale
= Orwell signals from line one that something is wrong: clocks don't strike thirteen.
